  "change": "Linear definitions with 17-128 steps check borrowed IDs using bounded local scratch and in-place sorting, with a strict-descending uniqueness fast path. Definitions with 1-16 steps retain the pairwise algorithm; size dispatch retains two common-path branches. No mutation, heap storage, wire/API/dependency changes.",
  "pilot_disposition": "Five-pair pilot exposed 20.61% short-ID and 29.23% long-ID reverse-17-step time regressions from small-sort behavior. Final source proves strict descending uniqueness before sorting; raw pilot retained.",
  "checks": {
    "parity": "Two properties at 10000 cases each on Rust 1.99 and 1.85: 40000 generated cases checked against frozen 5201529 pairwise validator; deterministic boundaries, precedence and reverse-path retry/compensation errors also pass.",
    "allocation": "42 isolated fixture validations per toolchain: 24 valid and 18 duplicate cases, across 1/16/17/128 steps, short/long IDs and ascending/descending/rotated ordering; zero allocations after setup.",
    "workspace": "Final-source all-target/all-feature suites on both toolchains excluding fuzz executable targets; strict workspace Clippy, warning-denied docs, doctests, formatting, layer boundaries, graph update passed.",
    "fuzz": "fuzz_linear_engine: 100000 runs seed 10 passed; not a rerun of the complete historical release campaign."
  },
  "measurement": "Final fixed 20 alternating revision pairs, seven binaries: 60 standalone validation fixtures and all six existing benchmarks. One warmup per binary/revision. CPU 0 serial, 0/1/2/3 parallel, Rust 1.99.0 bench profile. Other host workloads, frequency and caches uncontrolled. No own checks ran during timed campaigns.",
  "process_records": 290,
  "scope": [
    "Validation fixtures are valid definitions in three fixed orderings with two ID lengths, at 1/2/4/8/9/16/17/32/64/128 steps. They do not establish an all-input timing bound.",
    "The 128-reference scratch holds 1024 bytes of elements on this 64-bit host and is isolated in an out-of-line helper. This is not a whole-frame stack bound; the portable core is unchanged.",
    "Per-case times are reported separately; perf counters for definition_validation cover the complete 60-fixture process and include untimed fixture setup.",
    "No new application-wide slowdown percentage or universal speed/noninferiority guarantee. Existing control medians and paired intervals are retained."
  ],
